    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2WvunRxqLgBGFzjJ85aXPfJ)_\n\n## Symptom\n\nCaps+Shift+; enters AeroSpace's service mode, but there is no way back out.\n\n## Likely cause\n\nThe service-mode `esc` binding was `['reload-config', 'mode main']`. AeroSpace runs the commands of a binding in order and stops at the first one that fails, so if `reload-config` fails (or reports an error), `mode main` never runs and the mode is stuck. This is a diagnosis from the config, not a reproduced bug (no Mac here).\n\n## Changes\n\n- `aerospace.toml`: `esc = ['mode main', 'reload-config']` (leave first, then reload).\n- `aerospace-keys.lua`: Caps Lock + Esc runs `aerospace mode main`, so there is a way out even when AeroSpace does not receive Esc. It uses the existing `bind` helper, so it works with the current hotkey layer and with the event-tap version in #310.\n- `aerospace.org`: kept in sync (the TOML block, the `esc` note, the key list).\n\n## To check\n\nAfter `git pull`, a Hammerspoon reload and `aerospace reload-config`: enter service mode with Caps+Shift+;, then try `Esc`, then again and try Caps+Esc. From Terminal, `aerospace mode main` always works. If neither exits, the Hammerspoon Console or `aerospace reload-config` output will show the real error; send it to me.\n\nNo CHANGELOG edit (nightly routine owns it).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAZg8pR9NBT6MCe97U)_",
